            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Water-soluble anionic substituted thioglucosides. Glucosinolates have a central C atom which is bonded via an S atom to a glycone group and via an N atom to a sulfonated oxime group, and which also carries a side-group. The side-chain and sulfate group have an &lt;i&gt;anti&lt;/i&gt; stereochemical configuration across the C=N double bond.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>kegg.compound:C17260</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>pubmed:17139450</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
