        <obo:IAO_0000115>A member of the class of pterocarpans that is (6a&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;,11a&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;)-6a,11a-dihydro-6H-[1]benzofuro[3,2-&lt;em&gt;c&lt;/em&gt;]chromene which is substituted by a hydroxy group at position 3, a second hydroxy group at position 6a (resulting in the CIP stereochemical designation changing to &lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;,&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;), and a methylenedioxy group at positions 8-9. It is a metabolite of the pea phytoalexin (+)-pisatin, produced by the pea-pathogenic &lt;em&gt;Fusarium oxysporum forma specialis pisi&lt;/em&gt;, and a number of other fungi, including &lt;em&gt;Fusarium anruioides&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Fusarium avenaceum&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Mycosphaerella pinodes&lt;/em&gt;, and &lt;em&gt;Stemphylium botryosum&lt;/em&gt;.</obo:IAO_0000115>
