        <obo:IAO_0000115>A  sapogenin that is spirostan which is substituted by a hydroxy group at the 3β position, contains a double bond at the 5-6 position, and has &lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;- configuration at position 25. A natural product found in &lt;em&gt;Dioscorea&lt;/em&gt; (wild yam) species, it is used as the starting point for the commercial synthesis of a number of steroids, including cortisone, pregnenolone and progesterone.</obo:IAO_0000115>
