        <obo:IAO_0000115>A proanthocyanidin consisting of (−)-epicatechin and (+)-catechin units joined by a bond between positions 4 and 8&apos; respectively  in a β-configuration.. Procyanidin B1 can be found in &lt;em&gt;Cinnamomum verum&lt;/em&gt; (Ceylon cinnamon, in the rind, bark or cortex), in &lt;em&gt;Uncaria guianensis&lt;/em&gt; (cat&apos;s claw, in the root), and in &lt;em&gt;Vitis vinifera&lt;/em&gt; (common grape vine, in the leaf) or in peach.</obo:IAO_0000115>
