    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_79316 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_79316">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_136440"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_79313"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000087"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_76924"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018034"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24279"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0018038"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_136442"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A glycosinolic acid derived from glucose. Glucosinolic acids have a central C atom which is bonded via an S atom to a glucosyl group and via an N atom to a sulfonated oxime group, and which also carries a side-group. The side-chain and sulfate group have an &lt;i&gt;anti&lt;/i&gt; stereochemical configuration across the C=N double bond.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>chebi_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>glucosinolic acids</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
